The files sdr2hdr-*.maclcnn hold the networks MacLC uses for the High and
Maximum levels of its SDR to HDR conversion. Each predicts, from a small
thumbnail of the picture, a bilateral grid of brightness gains that the
video output applies to the full-resolution picture.

Hazen Studio designed and trained these networks for MacLC. They are part of
MacLC and are distributed under the same terms as the module that loads them,
the GNU Lesser General Public License, version 2.1 or later.

Training data: high dynamic range photographs from Poly Haven
(https://polyhaven.com/hdris), published under CC0 1.0, from which pairs of
standard and high dynamic range pictures were simulated. Thanks to Poly Haven
and its contributors.

File format: the magic "MLCNN001", a little-endian 32-bit length, a JSON
header describing the layers, then the weights as 16-bit floats
(modules/video_output/apple/VLCHDRNetwork.m reads it).
